==============================================================================
                    LM STUDIO MULTI-MODEL ORCHESTRATOR
==============================================================================

OVERVIEW
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LM Studio Multi-Model Orchestrator is a Python/Tkinter desktop application 
designed to control, interact with, and pipeline local Large Language Models 
(LLMs) hosted via LM Studio's local HTTP REST API. 

The application offers dynamic model switching, real-time token tracking, an 
interactive single-model chat interface, and a 5-pass "Story Cascade" engine 
for iterative content creation and multi-model refinement.


KEY FEATURES
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Automatic LM Studio Connection:
  Connects to default local server endpoints at http://localhost:1234.

* Dynamic Model Discovery & Loading:
  Lists available local LLMs along with their quantization information, 
  allowing on-demand loading via double-click actions.

* 5-Pass Story Cascade Engine:
  Chains up to 5 custom-assigned models to generate and refine text:
    - Pass 1 (Create) : Drafts initial story from prompt (~300-400 words).
    - Pass 2 (Refine) : Enhances narrative flow and descriptive details.
    - Pass 3 (Refine) : Deepens character development and dialogue.
    - Pass 4 (Refine) : Adjusts pacing, tension, and structure.
    - Pass 5 (Polish) : Refines prose to publication quality.

* Flexible Per-Pass Configurations:
  Assign individual models and set maximum token limits (100–4000 tokens) 
  independently for each pass in the cascade.

* Built-in Single Model Chat:
  Simple chat interface with message bubbles for quick testing. Supports 
  keyboard shortcut sending (Ctrl + Enter).

* Session & Reasoning Token Counter:
  Tracks total token consumption across sessions as well as reasoning tokens 
  used in individual API calls.

* File Management & Logging:
  - Writes runtime logs automatically to ~/Downloads/lm_studio_logs.txt.
  - Exports completed cascade stories to ~/Downloads/ with timestamped filenames.

* Lockable Resizable GUI:
  Standard starting size (900x624) with live resolution readouts and a toggle 
  window-lock mechanism (🔒/🔓).


PREREQUISITES & REQUIREMENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Operating System : Windows, macOS, or Linux
* Python           : Version 3.7+ (Tkinter included in standard installations)
* Dependencies     : 'requests' library
* LM Studio        : Downloaded, installed, and running with Local Server enabled


INSTALLATION & QUICK START
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Clone or download this repository:
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/lm-studio-orchestrator.git
   cd lm-studio-orchestrator

2. Install Python dependencies:
   pip install requests

3. Launch LM Studio:
   - Go to the Local Server tab ('<->' icon).
   - Confirm server port is set to 1234.
   - Click "Start Server".

4. Run the Orchestrator:
   python LMmultipass.py


VERIFIED API ENDPOINTS USED
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The application interfaces with LM Studio using the following REST endpoints:

Method   Endpoint                 Purpose
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET      /api/v1/models           Checks server connection and fetches 
                                  available LLM models & metadata.
POST     /api/v1/models/load      Loads selected model into local memory.
POST     /v1/chat/completions     Executes chat messages and story cascade 
                                  generations.


GUI LAYOUT & STRUCTURE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Model Control Card:
  Shows status indicators for server connection and active model, global max 
  token/temperature options, session token counters, resolution readouts, 
  and application refresh/restart controls.

* Model Management Card:
  Displays available LLMs. Double-click any model entry to trigger a load request.

* Story Cascade Card:
  Configures seed prompts, model assignments for Passes 1-5, per-pass token 
  limits, global cascade temperature, and controls output generation/saving.

* Chat Card:
  Provides a quick chat interface with dropdown model selection, text field, 
  and history clearing options.
